          <Pad Id="IEAxQFCDA7aLdSlHGcj41d" Bounds="1025,1829,415,239" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="NOTE:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Please note that a texture is not an image. They are similar, but they are not the same. A texture resides in the memory of the graphics card (GPU), whereas an image resides in the memory of the CPU. As a result, they may behave differently and cannot always be used interchangeably.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;For the next step, the texture needs to be transferred from the GPU to the CPU. During this process, it is also converted from Stride (the 3D game engine) to Skia (the 2D rendering engine). This is what this node does.&#xD;&#xA;">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
