          <Pad Id="KfVZDjc3ENsN8FejqGv5PN" Bounds="-770,2214,383,215" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Textures are powerful to work with. There are many additional nodes that provide Photoshop-like effects and image-processing operations.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Take a look at the help patches for examples. Typically, these effects are used to create more artistic or stylised visuals, which would not work in this particular case.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;However, there is one interesting example on the left that is worth exploring... again click on the node, press F1 for help... &#xD;&#xA;">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
